# The image builds realty-rest from source, so the context needs the sources,
# the Gradle wrapper and the build scripts -- and nothing else.
#
# Excluding every .gradle directory is not just about size: the Gradle daemon
# holds an exclusive lock on files under buildSrc/.gradle while it is running,
# and a running dev Minecraft server holds one on realty-paper/run/world/
# session.lock. Docker's context sender aborts the whole build when it cannot
# read a file, so anything either of them writes is excluded, at any depth.
**/.gradle
**/.kotlin
**/build
.git
.gitignore
.claude
.idea
**/run
docs
memory-bank
*.md
compose*.yml
